2.
Definitions.
- In these Regulations unless the context otherwise requires :-
(a)
"Act" means the Navy Act, 1957 (
62 of 1957
);
(b)
"Active list" except in Chapter XIII means the list of officers of the Indian Navy other than those who are placed on the
"retired list" or "emergency list";
(c)
"Appendix" means an Apendix to these regulations;
(d)
"Captain" means the officer appointed to command a ship;
(e)
"Emergency list" means the list entitled as such on which officers are placed
(i)
In accordance with Chapter X of these Regulations; and
(ii)
In accordance with any other regulations in force for the time being;
(f)
"General list" means the list of officers in the Indian Navy who are holding the rank of Acting Sub-Lieutenant or above,
excluding officers on the special Duties list;
(g)
"General service" means service in the Indian Navy other than in any specialist capacity;
(h)
"Government" means the Central Government;
(i)
"Navy order" means an order issued by the Chief of the Naval staff;
(j)
"Retired list" means the list entitled as such on which officers holding permanent commissions are placed when they
retire from the Service with pension or gratuity;
(k)
"Service" means Indian Naval Service;
(l)
All words and expressions used but not defined in these Regulations and defined in the Act shall have the meanings
respectively assigned to them in the Act.
